From c07378d51066fa99397a5c55c7568d601f2e1d84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom McDonald <214910594+tamcdonald42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:09:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix $4210 NMI latch starvation that deadlocked the FF6
 prologue

The NMI handle/r's own ack read cleared rdnmiPending, and the beam driver
runs the handler immediately on reaching v=225, so the handler always beat
the main loop's 'lda hRDNMI / bpl' poll. Every frame the poll saw pend=0 on
all reads and spun forever; the event VM never advanced past the $F0
'play song' command and the screen stayed blank from frame 5080.

A read taken while inNmi now acks the interrupt without consuming the
pending latch. Verified against bsnes accuracy (snesref oracle): recomp vs
reference WRAM at frame 5200 went from 13006 bytes apart (permanent) to 80,
with identical event state, and a cold boot now reaches the Narsay opening
mission through the title screen.
---
